        "description": "It is believed that maternal self-confidence is an important factor to provide good infant care and understanding their needs. 33 In view of this, a study has been conducted in Iran to explore the role of educational package on functional status and maternal self-confidence among the women during postpartum period. 34 The trial included 136 primiparous women for their second postpartum care. Four sessions of training, each commencing at 10–15 days postpartum, were conducted, whereas the health facilities provided regular postpartum care and training to the control group.",
