        "description": "Taking at least six weeks of leave can help you recover from childbirth and settle into a good breastfeeding routine. <strong>Practice expressing your milk by hand or with a breast pump several days or weeks before you have to go back to work</strong>. It can feel very different to pump breastmilk compared ...",
