        "description": "Below, we’ll discuss the importance of pumping at work, which generally allows employees to maintain milk production and feeding schedules at home, build up their breast milk supply, and relieve pressure or discomfort in breasts. Breastfeeding mothers also see faster rates of postpartum healing, stronger maternal bonds with their babies, and additional health benefits, including lower rates of high blood pressure, heart disease, diabetes, and more.",
